IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ap-dates`
IMPORT `ap-duties`
IMPORT `ap-survival`
IMPORT `ap-seat`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions on s 29 and s 30 (ap-seat.l4) and
-- the date helpers (ap-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the
-- encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: s 29 and s 30`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates`

-- 3 months on from 30 November 2026 is 28 February 2027 (no 30 February, fork F1); 6 months on from 31 August 2027 is
-- 29 February 2028 (a leap year); 12 months on from 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 30 `days after` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 31 3 2027
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 2 2028) `to` (`d` 2 3 2028) EQUALS 30

§§ `s 29(1) -- does the claim survive`

#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `a dependants' claim under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `defamation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `seduction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3 and the First Schedule -- dust-related condition`

#ASSERT `Is the illness a dust-related condition` `Mesothelioma` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the illness a dust-related condition` `Silicosis` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the illness a dust-related condition` `Farmers' lung` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the illness a dust-related condition` `another pathological condition of the lungs, pleura, peritoneum or sinus` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the illness a dust-related condition` `another pathological condition of the lungs, pleura, peritoneum or sinus` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the illness a dust-related condition` `a condition of another kind` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 29(2), (2A), s 99AC -- what the estate may recover`

-- Arguments: kind, head, death caused by the wrong, condition, attributable to dust, condition caused by the wrong,
-- proceedings pending at death, day proceedings started, day of death.
-- A worker died of mesothelioma caused by the employer's negligence, with proceedings started before death and pending.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `bodily or mental harm` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `the curtailment of expectation of life` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `included`
-- No proceedings pending at death: (2)(c)(ii) excludes it.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
-- Not a dust-related condition, or the condition not caused by the wrong.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `a condition of another kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Asbestosis` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `another pathological condition of the lungs, pleura, peritoneum or sinus` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `included`
-- s 99AC: commenced before 10 May 2000 and died before it: (2A) does not apply; died on 10 May 2000 or later: it does.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Asbestosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2000) (`d` 9 5 2000) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Asbestosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2000) (`d` 10 5 2000) EQUALS `included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Asbestosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 9 5 2000) (`d` 10 5 2000) EQUALS `included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Asbestosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 5 2000) (`d` 1 6 2000) EQUALS `included`
-- The other heads where the death was caused by the wrong.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `exemplary damages` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `funeral expenses` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `may be included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `future probable earnings had the person survived` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `loss of earning capacity for a period after the death` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `any other loss suffered before the death` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `s 29 does not limit it: the general law of damages decides`
-- Death from another cause: s 29(2)(c) does not reach the heads; exemplary damages are still out.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `pain or suffering` FALSE `a condition of another kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `s 29 does not limit it: the general law of damages decides`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `funeral expenses` FALSE `a condition of another kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `s 29 does not limit it: the general law of damages decides`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a claim for injury, loss or damage of any other kind` `exemplary damages` FALSE `a condition of another kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a dependants' claim under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958` `exemplary damages` FALSE `a condition of another kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `defamation` `pain or suffering` TRUE `Mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `the cause of action did not survive, so nothing is recoverable for the estate`

§§ `s 29(3) -- suing the estate of the person liable`

-- Arguments: tort, started before their death, last day had they lived, out of time at death, representation taken out,
-- day of representation, personal injury claim, court allowed longer period, last day of longer period, day I start.
-- Last day had they lived 30 June 2027; representation 1 February 2027, so six months run to 1 August 2027.
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 2 8 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No representation yet: after the last day had they lived, no route.
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Out of time at death: (c) is closed.
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Proceedings started before the death and pending: (a).
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A court's longer period for a personal injury claim: (b)(ii), to its last day.
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 31 12 2028) (`d` 31 12 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 31 12 2028) (`d` 1 1 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 31 12 2028) (`d` 1 6 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not in tort: s 29(3) does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can I sue the estate of the person liable to me` FALSE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `By when must I sue the estate` (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `the last day is` (`d` 1 8 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I sue the estate` (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the last day is` (`d` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I sue the estate` (`d` 30 6 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `the last day is` (`d` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I sue the estate` (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `the last day is` (`d` 29 2 2028)
#ASSERT `By when must I sue the estate` (`d` 30 6 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `six months after representation is taken out, and at least until` (`d` 30 6 2027)

§§ `s 30 -- the executor's notice to take proceedings`

#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings after the executor's notice` (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings after the executor's notice` (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings after the executor's notice` (`d` 30 11 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028

-- Notice received 15 March 2027; the last day is 15 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Have I taken proceedings in time after the executor's notice` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Have I taken proceedings in time after the executor's notice` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Have I taken proceedings in time after the executor's notice` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 16 6 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Have I taken proceedings in time after the executor's notice` (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 6 2027) EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Have I taken proceedings in time after the executor's notice` (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 6 2027) EQUALS `not done in time`
